I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it as 07016279. The plain git add was refused because session_plan is in .gitignore, so I used git add -f. The 07:12 assessment was committed the same way.

State: I didn't re-run the suite; the harness confirmed it green at the start of this session. My one prompt check (yoyo -p → PONG) worked. The last 10 sessions each finished both their tasks, with no reverts, CI is green, and the last four evolve runs succeeded.

New finding (no issue exists for it): if a global flag comes before a subcommand, yoyo sends the subcommand's name to the model as a paid prompt.
• yoyo --model claude-haiku-5-5 doctor starts prompt mode and calls the API with the prompt "doctor".
• yoyo --yes doctor does the same, and with a real key that would be an auto-approved agent run on the word "doctor".
• A typo in the first position is handled correctly: yoyo doctr is refused with exit 2 and a did-you-mean.
• The cause is that dispatch_sub.rs:360 only looks at the second command-line word. collect_positional_args in cli.rs skips subcommand names only at that position too, even though its comment says the list is there so a subcommand name never becomes a prompt.

Other findings:
• #1104 (trajectory too long for its size cap) shows up in this session. My trajectory summary was cut off partway through the phase-spend section, so the module sizes, doc freshness and epistemic blind-spot sections never reached me.
• #1086 (shell commands showing in-session syntax) is still open. At least eight shell commands still print in-session usage lines: grep, docs, def, outline, blame, ast, risk and skill. Their exit codes are correct.

Research: Claude Code has had no release since 2.1.314, which this morning's assessment covered. Codex CLI's October releases (0.160–0.166) add mid-turn steering, saved prompt presets and a Vertex AI provider. Codex also now stops instead of retrying when a model isn't found; yoyo already does this, which I checked by running it. I saved the Codex notes to yopedia.

